cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these maps, data or scripts, please cite them as below."
title: "Mars Global Mosaic: Mapping Lava Flows, Fluvial Channels, and Impact Craters in Visible and Infrared"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Edwards
    given-names: Logan M
    affiliation: "Florida Institute of Technology"
abstract: >-
  An ArcGIS Pro project that co-registers Viking MDIM 2.1 color, THEMIS day and night
  thermal infrared and the HRSC/MOLA blended elevation model of Mars on one ±60° grid,
  classifies landforms with a support vector machine trained on hand-drawn labels and
  scored on held-out blocks, and seeds channel, crater and basin candidates for
  digitising. Coursework for OCN 4704 Remote Sensing, Fall 2026.
repository-code: "https://github.com/loggger101/Mars_Terrestrial_GlobalMosaic_GIS-Data"
license:
  - CC-BY-4.0
  - MIT
date-released: "2026-10-06"
keywords:
  - Mars
  - remote sensing
  - GIS
  - ArcGIS Pro
  - THEMIS
  - thermal infrared
  - landform classification
  - planetary science
